          "blockId": "BLK_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_017FC3AC_CONCEPTS_01_CONSERVATIVE_FORCES",
          "semanticAnchorId": "ANCHOR_CONSERVATIVE_FORCES",
          "title": "1. Conservative Forces and Potential Energy Relation",
          "contentMarkdown": "A force is conservative if work done is path-independent. Potential energy $V(x)$ relates to conservative force by $$F(x) = -\\\\frac{dV(x)}{dx}$$, meaning $$\\Delta V = -W_{\\\\text{conservative}}$$. Gravitational potential energy near Earth is $$V(h) = mgh$$.",
